window.products.push({"id":223552,"name":"Tiki Large HANDCRAFTED wooden wall clock hawaiian style Maori mythology home decor for bedroom kitchen living room and office decoration art, original","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71eRRy5my4L._SL1500_.jpg","description":"Handcrafted wooden wall clock In Māori mythology, Tiki is the first man, created by either Tūmatauenga or Tāne. He found the first woman, Marikoriko, in a pond; she seduced him and he became the father of Hine-kau-ataata. By extension, a tiki is a large or small wooden or stone carving in humanoid form, although this is a somewhat archaic usage in the Māori language. Carvings similar to tikis and coming to represent deified ancestors are found in most Polynesian cultures. They often serve to mark the boundaries of sacred or significant sites. (c) wiki Wood: baltic birch Coating: acrylic paints, varnish, wood stain Size: 32x16 cm *AA battery is not included **the clock hands can slightly differ from those on the pics","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71eRRy5my4L._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"WOODANDROOT","source_asin":"B074MCDV38","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-223552","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B074MCDV38","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B074MCDV38","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
